invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_sign64_sp1 returns without wiping the modulus record of p, so
  the prime and R^2 modulo it stay in the dead frame after every
  signature, and a later caller's uninitialized stack reads the key. No
  output changes, so no vector notices. bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test copies
  the stack below one call and requires no two words side by side of the
  prime in the copy.

--- old
    ct_wipe(&mod_p, sizeof mod_p);
    ct_wipe(&mod_q, sizeof mod_q);
--- new
    ct_wipe(&mod_q, sizeof mod_q);
